Notebook[{
Cell["Trajectories, the Record, and the Master Equation", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"dbfe112a-f03b-4140-bd09-33990ebe1887"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Simulating the stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger \
equation of a free particle under continuous weak position measurement in the \
Wolfram Language. Continuous homodyne detection produces a stochastic \
measurement record; conditioning the state on that record unravels the \
Lindblad master equation into individual quantum trajectories, each a pure \
conditional state undergoing measurement-induced localization; and averaging \
the conditional states over the measurement noise recovers the unconditional, \
decohering master-equation state. Every simulated quantity is matched to an \
observable of a continuous-measurement experiment.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"346d34e2-3c40-4f8b-908f-\
f51bc65bc66c"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: July 28, 2026)", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8d2775ba-f1b7-4f6d-bf24-d03edc05afd3"],

Cell["Setting the Stage", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4a3d792a-1ae1-4fa4-8dcf-42f9e7511c72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is a companion to ",
 StyleBox["Watching a Quantum Particle", "TI"],
 ", which derives the stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation (SSE) of \
continuous position measurement. Here I take the SSE as given and answer one \
question: how does the simulation connect to a real experiment? The answer \
has three parts, and the document is built around them. Continuous homodyne \
detection produces a stochastic ",
 StyleBox["measurement record", "TI"],
 ". Conditioning on one record yields one ",
 StyleBox["quantum trajectory", "TI"],
 ", a pure conditional state whose mean diffuses and whose variance \
localizes. Averaging the conditional states over the measurement noise, or \
equivalently discarding the record, returns the ",
 StyleBox["unconditional state", "TI"],
 ", which obeys the Lindblad master equation and decoheres. One trajectory is \
the a-posteriori state inferred in a single run; the unconditional state is \
the a-priori ensemble that remains when the record is not read."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee85b23f-7d56-489b-9153-ea5c0403fef2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every number below is produced by a cell you can rerun and change. This is \
a live notebook, so evaluate the cells top to bottom and vary the measurement \
strength, the initial state, and the ensemble size. I assume basic quantum \
mechanics and working Wolfram Language; no stochastic calculus is needed \
beyond the defining property of the Wiener process, that its increment over a \
step of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b1a35f81-c1d6-4f43-b340-0f9590e943cd"],
 " is a zero-mean Gaussian of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "81ff05f8-7884-4c8c-88ec-4a357e9810f3"],
 ". Throughout, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f317eda-ec07-491f-9c55-385be9ac12f5"],
 ", the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e21b84c-15de-414d-afad-64f0f7861ab1"],
 ", and the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37270ab1-1fa3-46d3-9c97-f828a60ad1dd"],
 " (equivalently the measurement rate) stay symbolic wherever the algebra is \
symbolic, and take numerical values (",
 Cell[BoxData["hbar"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "be3f6b08-0f02-4ff8-85a3-ae9a1cd3ae32"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["mass"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aadbc44-e120-46c2-834d-b90eb4eaf53a"],
 ") only in simulation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f7952f14-2b72-4979-ab94-dfddb658f7fa"],

Cell["Part I: The Equation and the Detector's Output", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bb3552aa-8573-4de3-b645-0f2000c0d318"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A particle with Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bcdec3ac-ecc2-457e-83c4-66605aa06a75"],
 " under continuous position measurement obeys"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d27d56d6-0969-4bc1-9e75-6b25898e6c52"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "2"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
           SpanMaxSize->1], 
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
           SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "]"}], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c131804b-b67e-4d64-\
9f6f-bc24e437a9d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three terms are the free unitary evolution under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bec808b-8197-45bc-af0c-bac652c392fe"],
 "; the stochastic backaction term proportional to the Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "096e9a7b-ca9a-4f1a-ab65-e8c19e457f98"],
 ", which conditions the state toward a more sharply defined position; and \
the nonlinear drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8bbf1891-df5a-4434-a206-08c20169573d"],
 ", which preserves the norm of the conditional state. In this diffusive, \
norm-preserving form the SSE is the quantum-state-diffusion (QSD) equation of \
Gisin and Percival. The Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13ae12ce-7ad0-44a7-b07d-6105514f4910"],
 " is the detector shot noise and, equivalently, the innovation of the \
associated quantum filter, and the same increment appears in the measurement \
record output by the detector,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a59bbe92-2b83-485f-a81f-df5222552c9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d06a89a1-6ffc-46d1-\
834d-33bb37313054"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The record is the conditional mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cf05875-941b-447c-859d-d52e80c146d5"],
 " superposed on white noise. This is precisely the output of a continuous \
position detector: the homodyne photocurrent of light scattered by the \
particle, or the voltage of a probe following its motion. Over one time step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a49ce6d2-5187-40c1-9f7e-60a2a90e5d6a"],
 " the detector returns one outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "184cbc27-7974-4f9e-9129-b0cd286e56db"],
 " of a weak position measurement, the state is acted on by the measurement \
(Kraus) operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17e28e0f-8fc5-40e1-b982-6023912de29a"],
 ", whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "177968cc-4160-45e8-9125-773b49178c4f"],
 " is the POVM element for outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a817c9f-576c-4fbd-8d89-a03a5849231b"],
 ", and renormalized, and it then evolves unitarily for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f470b405-ecdc-4d36-b7c3-f79736faff7b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d0e0d1b8-6a0a-496e-9760-3b7f505f7871"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
       "Ket"]}], GridBox[{
       {GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
            RowBox[{
             StyleBox["(",
              SpanMaxSize->1], 
             OverscriptBox[
              StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
             StyleBox[")",
              SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
            TemplateBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
                StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
                StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
                StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
             "Ket"]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]], "."}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b47dc409-288c-476a-\
b7f3-70dc12adff6e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The SSE is exactly the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d70883d2-e8b0-4af3-9252-f88b2e8393fc"],
 " limit of this conditional update, with the outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c79f4e85-3a00-4ab8-9ef4-8662735be057"],
 " distributed according to the measurement probability density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {GridBox[{
        {
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
          TemplateBox[{
            StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
           "Ket"]}]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "351c6179-fbe1-4b0a-986d-ff68d2e63d74"],
 ": it is the equation of motion for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3e80bed-f64a-48dd-8636-0e941e68ddf5"],
 " conditioned on the record, and its nonlinearity, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d98cee8-b9b8-4bc3-b694-f4fbd6ea8608"],
 " terms, is exactly the cost of the renormalization by ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["(",
           SpanMaxSize->1], 
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
          StyleBox[")",
           SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
         TemplateBox[{
           StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
          "Ket"]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fb779895-c5db-481a-a78c-948d1b515d06"],
 ". Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1d52305-bf4b-4e14-9bf8-df7c6bc511b7"],
 " is unitary it preserves the norm, so the split ordering used in the code, \
measure then evolve, requires only the single normalization shown. The \
measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bf587d57-2e54-4490-ba2d-2cfd048f06d2"],
 " sets the information rate of each weak measurement: larger ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "951a7410-c4e4-43b1-b656-aae77bfff29f"],
 " gives a sharper, more informative outcome and stronger measurement \
backaction."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"551166d4-f63e-4a41-84c5-fd82905637f6"],

Cell["Glossary", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b3dcba11-43e2-4048-99f8-42af1a81573d"],

Cell["\<\
The six symbols of Part I and their operational status. The last column \
states whether each is measurable, and if so how; the essential point is that \
only the record is measured, while the conditional mean is inferred from it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b178773e-c101-4a28-9b18-e8972a3c7063"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Symbol", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"b25d5e48-5456-4b44-a533-f608f127ff4e"],
     Cell["Meaning", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"14e83116-f32d-4b0f-ad15-1913beccbf44"],
     Cell["Observable, and how it is tested", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"733cf4b5-dccf-43f1-a371-c218275a89db"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "fd6ae198-2528-4f11-946f-58b04aee07c3"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "00e2edb5-cdd0-4940-8def-e63978e66c11"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the integrated measurement record, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "09b79c9d-b7e7-4a6e-ad35-66961d2dbc56"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"d20413c2-5a9d-4165-aca8-9724b56a5e90"], 
    Cell["Directly observed: the (integrated) homodyne photocurrent.", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"15b69155-bd49-4581-8d74-1ce8a8a98a75"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "3b668732-273f-46fe-8a3f-5ed2103d2c06"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "44d8532d-8ce3-4411-bd78-c9ff8b4980ec"], Cell[
    "one weak-measurement outcome per step", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3dbcc9b1-2f3f-445c-a056-db92cd2c2a4b"], Cell["\<\
Directly observed; a single outcome has signal-to-noise below one.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"abd08998-cc23-4475-ab11-1e4b19c71ddd"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "6a1aaced-19ac-4aaf-825b-4890eba13942"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4c913543-0f54-4363-8a0c-9b17d16a6c82"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the Wiener increment, the detector shot noise, equal to the innovation ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "-", "2", 
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "246e0d1e-e78d-4553-95f1-8b96594f01f8"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"67a9a38b-317e-4cc9-83ce-7c37cd1e76c2"], 
    Cell[TextData[{
     "Recoverable once ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "0d259093-b226-407d-988f-cf22df2b4fb2"],
     " is estimated: the record minus its conditional mean."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"204dd87a-9f2c-494b-b88e-a840d0c09b6e"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "ff36b135-d39d-4b8a-8306-dcc69a935b5e"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "be185cf2-1c3c-40fe-80a9-10f22b025d00"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the conditional mean position, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Integral]",
        FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["(",
             SpanMaxSize->1], 
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
            StyleBox[")",
             SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "2ff1dff3-e6a1-458d-9985-9df93e1b5df0"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"823bb8b3-100e-4e73-b725-0a28da3ad79f"], 
    Cell["\<\
Not a single-shot readout; the filtered position estimate (the red curve), \
tested as the estimator output and used in feedback.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"88414a06-378b-4956-b419-e6ba1f7c04ca"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "622ffc9f-91ca-45e1-8864-c976039c8351"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "eb2c23c0-3b8b-4e17-896b-5893b602ae07"], Cell[
    "the position operator, the measured observable", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"81b5a53a-6edf-4d7a-8a74-77d135c6e1d3"], Cell["\<\
Observable: its weak-measurement outcomes are what the detector samples.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b00f0de7-a285-432d-93d6-ae292e004f91"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "80818eaa-08c6-440d-8ef3-91ec26523a26"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f6e932c7-d928-4fbd-baf0-f73927320461"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the Kraus (measurement) operator, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"\[Proportional]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           RowBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "8ec7f7ab-5ee4-4ad4-b901-a5cfee53d6c6"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3e034382-e234-4596-bec0-b0eca2a4bd21"], 
    Cell["\<\
Not observable; it defines the measurement update and the outcome statistics.\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1a2b8525-b873-4548-b447-7efa38e05c70"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.14], 
      Scaled[0.37], 
      Scaled[0.37]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",Express\
ionUUID->"dd170d55-098f-4a7c-819c-89b9ecfe05cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Only the record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca48ae7c-5fe3-4e55-beb8-17a06b68a697"],
 ", through its outcomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26b38361-e7b3-45a6-b2da-a9e09b53b43d"],
 ", is measured; the conditional mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46b79ada-65d1-4252-95a8-ef28ad06564b"],
 " is inferred from it by filtering, which is exactly what Part VIII shows a \
real experiment doing in real time."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76e0114b-97db-406f-87a1-6152fa45b3a3"],

Cell["Part II: How to Simulate It", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"242c175d-bcd3-42e5-b4ed-8521ff16af42"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We build this on a position grid, one piece at a time. First fix units, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64255ed8-2f68-4c53-8cd7-dc88c9ac4555"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a5139575-f70e-40ed-b4ee-873714d815f7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mass", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c505bc5f-936e-41e9-afcb-3accd58e698b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The computational grid holds the position samples and the matching momenta \
in the wrapped ordering ",
 Cell[BoxData["Fourier"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "315d0012-c702-4cfd-aeff-790e991faef0"],
 " uses (nonnegative frequencies first, the negative half rotated to the \
end). The two arguments are ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5179009c-0f2d-4ba3-be63-737243ec8b35"],
 ", the number of grid points, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["ll"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b3952cc-2f39-4891-9cef-6ca6df835d0a"],
 ", the box length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "530d6da1-8a8e-47ee-921d-a0d2f618f4c9"],
 "; the returned association carries the spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a225c23f-818b-43ca-9c16-7ade002c2bdc"],
 " under ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<dx\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f115cc7-0cbe-4001-ba88-4ca64770b2c8"],
 ", the positions under ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<x\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a4938c9-1b26-4f38-b278-1bce4e0c119d"],
 ", and the momenta ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["integers",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8dcb59cf-b234-4699-9497-775f5fa2cba8"],
 " under ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<p\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba2a3c1a-bc9a-430f-8baf-92285bafba00"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5769a33-9ef1-4771-bddd-933c26817a4e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "ll_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ll", "/", "n"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<dx\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "dx"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dx", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "/", "ll"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"RotateLeft", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7d09b2ac-2532-4908-b790-bc9881c07f9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A normalized Gaussian wave packet on grid ",
 Cell[BoxData["g"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34118b9a-2b67-49b6-86a7-3f53f8b0a799"],
 ", of position width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "da595e91-c8c7-4669-a674-ffbf79968854"],
 " (so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae07441-4a8d-4b0e-bd0e-0a2b1563dd8b"],
 "), centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e8d84db1-0662-470c-90e9-a5cf84501dae"],
 " with mean momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4991f024-2b86-4a04-85bb-a26537b5aa74"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c480d943-f4b5-4de1-bd18-948f2956d736"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "x0_", ",", " ", "p0_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "x0"}], ")"}],
          "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "/", "hbar"}]}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f90f040f-2f70-49de-a302-e963c2ee5949"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Free unitary evolution of the wavefunction ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Psi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66366da9-df32-4ba4-9c34-4f2f2dd846b6"],
 " on grid ",
 Cell[BoxData["g"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fc6ef118-fb5b-4d2d-90bc-0a4ffab96d36"],
 " for a step ",
 Cell[BoxData["dt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7da7e9e6-faa0-4832-9edc-1d9415166d59"],
 " is diagonal in momentum, so it is a split-operator (Fourier) step: forward \
transform, multiply by the kinetic propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb97f59f-a52f-4538-bffe-1941cb119357"],
 ", inverse transform:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8bd7b8d6-beeb-4d20-878a-8aef37b3a0bf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0ac37a3a-fd0b-4cdf-9aa6-2dc9e991df2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8303cc9-cd76-4bdb-bb3d-cbe6001e370d"],
 " is the inner product of the grid positions with the probability density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c975ea1-cd48-4e1f-82ea-0d7d911fe90e"],
 " (arguments: grid ",
 Cell[BoxData["g"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "005641c2-8a04-4cd0-84b9-9399bb57aea1"],
 ", wavefunction ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Psi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c59f411-a960-4998-b7f4-2cdd893ad7b7"],
 "):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c3d52a9-da32-45cd-aa01-48a4c21d65e9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e15ab5c0-92ac-4398-ba00-b2eaddbddbaa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and the conditional position variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ff56b623-981a-492f-af0b-2f77dd8f9547"],
 " is the second moment minus the square of the first:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48d6082e-4822-487e-be69-4ebc1101776c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ef5c9b4b-4e71-4294-bad4-09436bf339cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A measurement outcome is sampled from the exact outcome distribution ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {GridBox[{
        {
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
          TemplateBox[{
            StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
           "Ket"]}]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b16802c-689d-4d4d-92bd-262c5aa0155d"],
 ": a point drawn from the density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a2eadd92-8073-452c-9e3f-d688fe8b5aea"],
 " and convolved with detector Gaussian noise of standard deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed9df500-12c6-4871-bfcd-9dbf938b05a9"],
 ". The arguments are the grid ",
 Cell[BoxData["g"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d442e5cd-dd86-467a-bfe0-a652135f58fe"],
 ", the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Lambda]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4304914e-337f-4d3d-8e85-656b93ba0eb7"],
 ", and the step ",
 Cell[BoxData["dt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a658053-c13d-4de4-9879-f0b736eae49b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6a0de245-7499-4735-9ab6-e1ad900f0afe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"29a6d985-bfb7-44d4-81bc-781f75ea37f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement update applies the Kraus operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8dbcc256-892f-473e-80d7-92b5ee4a54e6"],
 " for outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData["xb"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "005edf8f-8877-4911-a551-28809d9189bd"],
 " and renormalizes the conditional state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"651c4fe3-f119-4fdd-9c40-1f0ec472bcc7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Lambda]"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], ")"}], 
        "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"028b6add-f5b6-4bcf-a9c9-e39fbb38b14b"],

Cell["\<\
and one full time step is the split conditional update from Part I, \
measurement followed by unitary evolution:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"97d0ba6a-a93d-4613-b9be-04879a010428"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "xb"}], 
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6869a9cc-8fa9-4ab6-b5fa-382a3032ecf5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One experimental run over ",
 Cell[BoxData["nt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72c8876d-d0ea-4944-9cea-65c309333a76"],
 " steps draws a measurement outcome at each step, records it, and propagates \
the conditional state from initial state ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Psi]0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1bad58d-dc7b-441f-b5cc-7e07d8f47c27"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reap"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dd0be90-2e43-4559-9430-bb39ebbf00c7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sow"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32dda900-bd60-4900-84d2-129ad6f871bd"],
 " accumulate the measurement record while ",
 Cell[BoxData["NestList"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96380cdf-80c6-43ce-ab29-e12dc710b135"],
 " accumulates the quantum trajectory:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d32c0a98-74cf-4af2-896c-c57a6020bc91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"expt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "nt_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Reap", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sow", "@", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
             RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[",
             "#", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
      "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"04e3b559-dae6-436d-b927-f4f81f3fe7bd"],

Cell["Part III: One Run Is One Experiment", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4c45e54b-d2f3-4e3c-bc67-767581723f8c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Simulate one run, starting from a broad packet so the measurement-induced \
localization is visible. Fix the grid, the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Lambda]R"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "89d463f8-2762-4b35-ba0b-d02acef32a16"],
 ", the step ",
 Cell[BoxData["dt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ee33f77-75c5-4d67-8375-a56667690d5f"],
 ", and the number of steps ",
 Cell[BoxData["nt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21b5dd6e-0439-422d-9ae6-e419b4288918"],
 ", and retain the full trajectory of conditional states and the measurement \
record:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"739a5605-18e5-46e9-a4b0-45e81a129711"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "50."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nt", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"states", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "record", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"expt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "nt"}], 
       "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"53baff82-9cbf-4f69-841b-9a53dfd21a54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Extract the conditional mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "854e90cf-51f1-461f-b467-360296cf91ad"],
 " and the conditional width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a7972-5ecb-47f2-b6c2-03a99f6a6495"],
 " along the trajectory:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3825e304-3ddd-4ca1-8f5c-b4606791d186"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xt", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "states"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"widths", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     "states"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"81f880f7-5522-425c-a81b-0d8304c07643"],

Cell["\<\
Check the step count, the localization of the width, and the purity of the \
final conditional state:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"abf8c07c-3a49-4d92-97c2-ca3ffddd9e82"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<steps\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\!\(\*SqrtBox[\\\"Vx\\\"]\): start -> end\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<purity of final state\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Length", "[", "record", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"First", "@", "widths"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "@", "widths"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ".", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Last", "@", "states"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Last", "@", "states"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6fd1cf09-6abf-47db-a5d6-d6cb2894f908"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "186e5ead-6492-472e-8b89-e8673b042b09"],
 " relaxes from ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47d2820a-bc2a-456e-92f2-5758093cb79f"],
 " to the steady value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"4", 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.71"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3af003fc-a6ab-4008-a09d-c9f936b237e3"],
 ", the square root of the steady conditional variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee3fcaa6-5585-4872-bdc6-b4d77324d6d7"],
 ", at which measurement-induced localization balances free dispersion, and \
the final conditional state is exactly pure. This is the defining property of \
an efficiently monitored trajectory: in a single run the particle occupies a \
definite, if randomly placed, pure state. Continuous observation does not mix \
the state; it localizes it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d840c74-9159-42a2-92cb-900594934765"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare the raw measurement record against the conditional mean inferred \
from it. The record is the gray point cloud; the conditional mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b37412c6-3ca7-418a-8ecc-d71efff8bdfa"],
 " estimated from it is the red curve:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bfa3073-6c21-4b28-88b6-f36819dcb3a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nt", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "record"}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.004", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "xt"}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<detector reading, and the mean \:27e8x\:27e9 you infer\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<One run: the noisy record (gray) and the trajectory it \
determines (red)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a1555068-1ce1-4893-b1af-d085d3987626"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The individual outcomes scatter over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "20"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bb4a84e-6d0f-4c5b-8c00-d62fcd98731f"],
 " while the particle remains within a few units of the origin: the \
signal-to-noise ratio of a single weak measurement is far below one. The \
conditional mean is recovered only after the measurement operator has \
integrated hundreds of outcomes. The record is the raw data; the trajectory \
is the estimate inferred from it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b6888ea-6557-4181-aa3a-231ae9d1a61c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is worth stating precisely what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08670564-706c-4a5f-b014-53a434f6ccb4"],
 " is, since the detector never reports it directly. It is the first moment \
of the conditional state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba01d27c-7cea-436d-9116-32808be8a93f"],
 ", the minimum-variance estimate of the position given the record so far. No \
single outcome is that estimate; a lone ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e54ebfb6-28a6-4e20-b3e9-94141efca103"],
 " has signal-to-noise below one, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed160dd0-b19a-4581-a482-7c3072d4b16b"],
 " is recovered only by propagating the full record through the conditional \
dynamics, which is what the trajectory does. It is worth tracking for three \
reasons: it is the signal carried by the record, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ceaa71b3-6476-4c9f-ad33-e332716328e9"],
 "; the particle is localized within ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd64e8ae-c0a3-445d-8dc7-43a1b346c915"],
 " of it, so the conditional mean and variance together specify the Gaussian \
state; and a feedback controller can act only on the estimate it computes in \
real time from the photocurrent, which is exactly this one. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7513f0bc-ecd0-4eca-b0d8-d66f33caa803"],
 " is not the eigenvalue of a single projective measurement but the filtered \
position estimate reconstructed from the continuous record, as physical as \
any conditional expectation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52488037-031d-4768-aa75-3227c3779ebd"],

Cell["\<\
The conditional width relaxes along the same deterministic curve in every run:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d63b518c-310f-4ffb-ae2f-edfb2c1919b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "widths"}], "}"}], 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<packet width \!\(\*SqrtBox[\\\"Vx\\\"]\)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The measurement sharpens the packet to a fixed width\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"12c6eb19-2293-4848-8be5-7222d3923687"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional mean and width are moments of the full conditional density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4e2a02d-7b8a-4c80-b036-b16d334b6d7e"],
 ", which is worth displaying directly and comparing between two runs. \
Restricting to the central region and reading time upward: both conditional \
densities localize to the same steady width, but each conditional mean \
follows an independent stochastic path, so the density ridge differs between \
runs."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b595cd15-4b54-4e1e-ab84-c990d7cdde63"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"band10", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{"10", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xr", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"First", "@", "band10"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "@", "band10"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"showDensity", "[", 
    RowBox[{"st_", ",", " ", "lbl_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "st", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ")"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "band10"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"xr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"nt", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1.4"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "250"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<t\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "lbl"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"states2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "4", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"First", "@", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"expt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "nt"}],
         "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"GraphicsRow", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"showDensity", "[", 
      RowBox[{"states", ",", " ", "\"\<run 1\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"showDensity", "[", 
      RowBox[{"states2", ",", " ", "\"\<run 2\>\""}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a06ddc90-42c8-4670-adac-dc6bbf2aa240"],

Cell["Part IV: Many Runs Are Many Possible Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c5350b86-dff5-4f80-aea3-8f5457fed649"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A different realization of the measurement noise produces a different \
trajectory. A helper returns the conditional-mean path ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae020a8f-7c83-4f78-95b8-e17495aeed9c"],
 " of one run:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4757d05-0011-40b6-9569-3a587675e025"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"pathX", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "nt_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
            RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
           "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
      "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5b113f6c-58b3-4840-b6ae-3b41999b6809"],

Cell["Simulate an ensemble of forty:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1dd52a5b-9b83-4c4e-b681-06825e1a60d5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"manyX", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "3", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"pathX", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}],
         "[", 
        RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}],
         "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "40", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5df99582-6260-463b-ac91-6fd8e6ee3ea7"],

Cell["\<\
Overlay the conditional means, one faint curve per realization:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a655756-adf3-4319-825e-3395d8026343"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "manyX"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<inferred mean \:27e8x\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Forty runs: each detector record sends the particle on its own \
walk\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ebab699e-786c-4591-a260-4fc9b0985257"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Those curves are the estimates; the underlying measurement records also \
differ from run to run. Each realization has its own outcome sequence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ec0e217-9636-4771-8bd5-bdb66407f81a"],
 " and its own integrated record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a86e9bc-c296-430b-a0de-669f908497e5"],
 ". The left panel shows the raw outcomes for three realizations, dominated \
by shot noise; the right shows the integrated record for thirty, in which the \
conditional-mean signal appears only as a slow drift beneath the Wiener \
(Brownian) spread."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"efd55295-b171-48b8-87f7-c786aa93f1db"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"manyRec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "3", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"expt", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "nt"}], 
          "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
          RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], 
          "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "30", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"manyY", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
    " ", "manyRec"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"GraphicsRow", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nt", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], 
          "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"manyRec", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.35", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.004", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<reading\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<three raw records\>\""}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "280"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nt", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], 
          "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "manyY"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<integrated record Y\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<thirty integrated records\>\""}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "280"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", "  ", 
    "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "600"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c03b02d6-b133-4f35-94fa-93a67d88ecaf"],

Cell["\<\
Each conditional mean follows an independent path and the ensemble spreads \
over several units. But at any fixed time all realizations share the \
identical conditional width, because the conditional variance obeys a \
deterministic (noiseless) equation while only the mean is driven by the \
record. To confirm that the ensemble spread of the means is large while that \
of the variances vanishes, take forty final conditional states:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"718f40ab-ee6c-4d6c-a61c-324c4ed7cabf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"finals", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "3", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
        RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
                RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], 
               "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
           RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], 
           "]"}], ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "40", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ca78f44b-0831-45d5-8176-e2a2d7c17714"],

Cell["\<\
and compare the ensemble standard deviation of the conditional means against \
that of the conditional variances:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4f11853-7c35-4f38-a19a-453893cb6ae6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<spread of centers \:27e8x\:27e9 across runs\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<spread of widths Vx across runs\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       "finals"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       "finals"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a6dc9854-e3a3-422b-948b-7c82a872db99"],

Cell["\<\
The conditional means scatter by several units; the conditional variances \
agree to fourteen digits. Every realization yields a differently centered \
conditional state of the same width. This is the outcome distribution \
obtained by repeating the experiment.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00443630-12f6-46dd-94dc-6f6f49ae8e21"],

Cell["Part V: Averaging Gives the Master Equation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"85332008-1488-4393-86dd-70498203237e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If the measurement record is discarded, or equivalently the conditional \
states are averaged over the measurement noise without post-selecting on \
their records, the description of the particle is the unconditional density \
matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Bra"]}], ")"}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "defed127-9c86-4d40-8344-4697295ab1de"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[CenterEllipsis]", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "928ff8e9-d946-4dab-a92b-8e10d671f374"],
 " denotes the ensemble average over the Wiener noise. This unconditional \
state obeys the Lindblad master equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"994560c8-728c-44c7-9282-fd26b465ae55"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["]",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"bb87652d-2c68-45a9-\
87d6-91e05d49dae2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the standard equation of spatial decoherence: the double-commutator \
dissipator suppresses off-diagonal coherence in the position basis at a rate \
set by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f306b04e-ae8b-42d1-80ff-008e77fdfd0c"],
 ". It integrates by the same operator split used for the trajectories. On \
the position grid the dissipator damps each element ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ac28841-e77e-4ee9-a3c6-c94bbc003ec1"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "-", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18a7a8cb-15be-426c-8779-131954cec083"],
 ", and the Hamiltonian part is the same free unitary evolution. Fix a grid \
",
 Cell[BoxData["gS"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "028019fe-1e02-4f1b-9438-a19e46370be7"],
 ", a step ",
 Cell[BoxData["dtS"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "361b3007-3ed2-4516-9640-bb27218bfa2e"],
 ", a horizon ",
 Cell[BoxData["tf"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d303d868-cc3d-4112-86ba-0360a541906a"],
 ", and the number of steps ",
 Cell[BoxData["ntS"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce109f97-89b3-4262-bda2-850651882288"],
 ", starting from an initial pure state ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Psi]0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b637275-a475-4214-977b-9921389cd7dc"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8d267d71-4ffd-4530-9c7d-7baeb71d721a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"32", ",", " ", "16."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dtS", " ", "=", " ", "0.0005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ntS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dtS"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"183fc213-1284-4bdf-93c0-ff837d31144d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dissipative step is one matrix of damping factors applied to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fdf9a71e-9dea-43d7-9e20-f21044200914"],
 " elementwise:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c3c007eb-eacf-41a7-acc9-db1251de010b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"decohere", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "&"}], 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gS", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gS", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "dtS"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"83367b99-363d-4a46-bc80-d21188f55b32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Hamiltonian step is the same split-operator propagator as before, \
assembled as a matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData["uni"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba4040ba-817c-4f1a-ab81-d0aef7357118"],
 " so it can act on both sides of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40945f63-b8b9-44ab-beb2-49021d35026f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34725444-46bf-4fec-bef6-14f5c84d2e79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"uni", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "dtS"}], "]"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "32", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e14969fb-1e17-4c03-b723-38ba9e021811"],

Cell["\<\
One master-equation step applies the dissipator, then the unitary:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ede858d5-1b35-49d6-83da-be43475221d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"lindStep", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"uni", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", "decohere"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uni", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"af251ab1-54ac-4f47-94a8-e4cda41ca020"],

Cell["Propagate from the initial pure state to the horizon:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"84d60acf-e64d-4d77-a21a-f4d4fa1beead"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]Master", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lindStep", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "@", "\[Psi]0"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ntS"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"64ddd6a9-cb15-49a5-a6e5-578ad27b613a"],

Cell["\<\
Now average many conditional trajectories on the same grid and compare. \
Simulate eight hundred realizations and retain the final conditional state of \
each:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d92aa867-d367-49d4-b7b1-25c79d01c442"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"finalsS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtS", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
               RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtS"}], "]"}],
               "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
         " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", "ntS"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "800", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"532bc3ef-3351-4348-94a2-324b0936547f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ensemble average is the unconditional density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Bra"]}], ")"}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8d46026-e690-4348-8c3f-9b4fd3bc565a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b737416-3c39-4ec6-9052-2bb8444b121e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]Avg", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", "finalsS"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b927879b-7a63-49ee-805e-04ea00780eff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To evaluate observables, represent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25311ff3-4fc8-4dd4-9311-6b1ec28bf09e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ef3f57fe-b91d-42e9-819f-860769dc9be0"],
 " as matrices on this grid, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b5daf85-ba5d-4512-b242-8964a1a8b5e1"],
 " diagonal and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38e4c9a8-afa5-4301-8f4d-07daf9884408"],
 " via the Fourier transform:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"294b26cb-2f0b-4fec-8726-eadbd5e55672"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xm", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gS", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"p2m", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"gS", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         
         RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "32", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"03a4c8ef-1077-4c24-afd4-a848adb9ee76"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A helper returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0585336c-6f2e-4821-a5b2-c9a27d4c61d7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32330b0e-d6bc-4dba-bd62-4e8cd40b1ad8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dbcc116-da97-489c-94bf-777a2c06bae0"],
 ", and the purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe112bea-c69d-4e3f-a31b-467e0eb0610d"],
 " from any density matrix:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05732119-1429-4e42-a8d0-cab3b0d30a4f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"observables", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], 
     ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "p2m"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"9750bf6b-b90c-439c-ba75-ab5110092883"],

Cell["\<\
Place the master-equation state and the trajectory ensemble average side by \
side:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fce29acd-26d8-4a72-a5ce-5e463aaf3fcb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"observables", "[", "\[Rho]Master", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"observables", "[", "\[Rho]Avg", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<master equation\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<800 trajectories\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<\:27e8x\:27e9\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8x\.b2\:27e9\>\"",
         ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8p\.b2\:27e9\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<purity\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3a5af80b-1626-4232-9c98-061985840498"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two agree to the Monte-Carlo sampling error of eight hundred \
realizations, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["800"], "\[TildeTilde]", "4", "%"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d24d2160-8751-4ddd-ad5f-0659c34f4ee9"],
 ". The ensemble average of the conditional states reproduces the \
unconditional master-equation state: this is the consistency condition of the \
trajectory unravelling. In the last column, the purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b4f483b-899c-4166-a274-7118a5dcf9c2"],
 " of the average is about ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.62"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dc278920-1cda-4d94-9f13-b816bdd8e4f0"],
 ", well below one, so the unconditional state is ",
 StyleBox["mixed", "TI"],
 ", yet every conditional trajectory is exactly pure. The mixed, decohering \
state of standard decoherence theory is precisely the ensemble average over \
these pure conditional trajectories, one of which is realized, and knowable, \
in each run."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66636d95-89dd-4e17-a63f-dee738367862"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The separation between conditional and unconditional purity develops in \
time. Each conditional trajectory remains pure, its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2eadf454-0a18-4ced-8ffd-e2e03a5d9b2c"],
 " fixed at ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b831d445-e164-43f9-a935-34bb19445bac"],
 "; the unconditional average decoheres, its purity decreasing from ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27b686b5-e033-4282-a37d-19f201414d79"],
 " toward ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[TildeTilde]", "0.62"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a1db25a4-4edb-4cd0-9916-5a679af7d5f3"],
 ". On one pair of axes, the constant line and the decaying curve are the \
entire content of decoherence as an ensemble average over pure conditional \
trajectories:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c205b51-bfc1-4f58-8d34-88c1fa42fe7e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"trajS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "gS", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtS", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
                RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtS"}], 
                "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
          ",", " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", "ntS"}], "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "25"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "300", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"purTimes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dtS", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "ntS", ",", " ", "25"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"purEns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
           "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"trajS", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "@", 
        RowBox[{"trajS", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"purTimes", ",", " ", "purEns"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"purTimes", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "@", "purTimes"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Gray"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<purity Tr(\[Rho]\.b2)\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<average over runs\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<each single run\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Pure trajectories, mixed average\>\""}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"428e4774-2ae3-4ad1-abfa-0b4cb4806485"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Is each simulated state physical? A conditional state is pure, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a16b754c-61c6-41ee-81bc-042c50e6661d"],
 " must be positive semidefinite with eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", "0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "be0225cc-c936-44fb-a24b-d78fcdd84d3a"],
 ", and the unconditional average ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ba6ef50-27c2-4ab6-9859-0b78943bc8e4"],
 " must be a valid density matrix: positive semidefinite, Hermitian, of unit \
trace. Take the smallest eigenvalue of each conditional projector, over a \
sample of realizations:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dc1157e2-610a-4f70-be78-3f2aaea6964d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"projMin", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"finalsS", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{";;", " ", "20"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4cce6dfd-66d1-4be4-9478-87286bf3d2bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and report the per-realization norm error, the smallest projector \
eigenvalue, and the unconditional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "016588b6-6d6d-4f7c-8563-eec500684a36"],
 "'s smallest eigenvalue, trace, and deviation from Hermiticity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f3b3304-7337-4ee6-8b72-ea14ac82c104"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<per-run \:2016\[Psi]\:2016 error\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<per-run |\[Psi]\:27e9\:27e8\[Psi]| min eigenvalue\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\[Rho] min eigenvalue\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Rho] trace\>\"", ",",
      " ", "\"\<\[Rho] Hermiticity error\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
         "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "finalsS"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Min", "@", "projMin"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "\[Rho]Avg", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "\[Rho]Avg", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]Avg", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "\[Rho]Avg", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3fd52d80-1e27-46b0-a52c-c51eb8ddb1b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every conditional state stays normalized to machine precision, no projector \
eigenvalue falls below zero by more than rounding (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", 
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "16"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f6fca1-24a2-4f80-9354-3e2ee9f87a0e"],
 "), and the unconditional average is a valid density matrix: positive \
semidefinite to the same precision, Hermitian, of unit trace. The \
split-operator scheme keeps each state exactly physical, because it applies \
the measurement as an exact Kraus operator and renormalizes, never admitting \
a negative probability."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a5c7890-d786-4d63-ab46-a935a8356ffb"],

Cell["\<\
The third column exhibits measurement backaction heating the particle. The \
heating rate is exactly computable: the moments close, and the momentum \
variance obeys an equation whose only measurement input is a constant \
diffusion source,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f1c01f6-1095-43fa-8bb1-0553aa0a0126"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"moments", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x2", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xp", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xp", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"p2", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x2", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "v0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"xp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"p2", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "q0"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x2", ",", " ", "xp", ",", " ", "p2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}],
      "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<\:27e8p\.b2\:27e9(t)\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", "moments"}], ")"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<\:27e8x\.b2\:27e9(t)\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", "moments"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5c924148-8c2c-4e8f-9c8f-89d350192da6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "0"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16f7c981-69e3-4b81-baca-b6f95d41d1c6"],
 ": continuous position measurement heats the momentum at the constant rate \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2881c394-f191-4b5d-a58e-ccf785d6ee11"],
 ", independent of the mass, the state, and the Hamiltonian. This is the \
measurement backaction demanded by the uncertainty principle as the cost of \
position information, and at these parameters it takes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9f6ace4-8e60-47ab-a933-1bfbed4c6186"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.25"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6467fb2b-cf4e-42db-a1d8-8905e70d093e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0.25", "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["f", "TI"]], "=", "0.65"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4854d94c-d8dc-438c-a3ee-1deac00ea218"],
 ", matching the master equation above. Increasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c135eb83-653b-46c8-bdf4-3d71df4b4544"],
 " increases the backaction heating without bound; only a sufficiently fine \
grid can represent the resulting momenta, and a coarse grid fails silently \
here."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fef332da-b14b-4065-a9c5-d032d6e12a2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the moment equations in hand, return to the ensemble of conditional \
means from Part IV. Their ensemble variance is not free: it is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3afb8e79-5187-40c5-bfb7-13661042c983"],
 ", the unconditional position variance minus the conditional one. This is \
the variance decomposition of the quantum filter, the total position variance \
splitting into the part resolved into the fluctuating conditional mean and \
the part remaining as the conditional variance, and both terms are the \
deterministic solutions above. The envelope around the ensemble is therefore \
not fitted, but read directly from the moment equations:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29551919-5873-45f0-ad25-22b97371f1cd"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]IV", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"v0IV", ",", " ", "q0IV"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]IV", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Psi]IV", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
    "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x2master", "[", "tt_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", "moments"}], " ", "/.", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"m", " ", "->", " ", "mass"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "\[Lambda]R"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "->", " ", "hbar"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"v0", " ", "->", " ", "v0IV"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"q0", " ", "->", " ", "q0IV"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", "tt"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"band", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x2master", "[", 
          RowBox[{"k", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"widths", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"k", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",",
         " ", "0."}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], 
        "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "manyX"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.25", "]"}], ",", " ", "Thin"}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "band"}], "}"}],
         "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "band"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<inferred mean \:27e8x\:27e9, with the predicted band\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The spread of estimates is \!\(\*SqrtBox[\\\"(\:27e8x\.b2\:27e9 \
- Vx)\\\"]\), from the moment equations\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"79065c2a-d905-4160-8cab-23b93f8e22f0"],

Cell["\<\
The band brackets the forty realizations to their Monte-Carlo scatter. The \
information content of the record, how tightly the conditional mean is \
determined and how far it fluctuates, is fixed in advance by the same moment \
equations that set the backaction heating.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63c8b616-a3b5-43f7-b02e-70db1712574f"],

Cell["Part VI: How Good Is the Simulation? A Builtin Cross-Check", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"89f0aa8d-e05c-4281-85a2-d76491332dc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The split-operator scheme is hand-written, and the way to validate it is to \
hand the same SSE to Wolfram Language's built-in stochastic integrator and \
check for agreement. ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dbee3576-21b3-4e3e-ac6c-088cbaaafaf9"],
 " represents an Ito stochastic differential equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18cf08e8-bbd2-41a6-856f-333ac59e0029"],
 " directly, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "902d8642-c420-43c4-a7f8-dc50c70ef8b8"],
 " integrates it. The built-in cannot use the spectral propagator, so the \
Hamiltonian is supplied as an explicit finite-difference kinetic-energy \
matrix, a tridiagonal second derivative with periodic boundary conditions \
(arguments: grid size ",
 Cell[BoxData["nn"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87acbc15-267a-4d2c-879c-569b2a536396"],
 ", spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData["dx"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "488f3fb2-7132-4be3-bb1a-12b3d735f4bb"],
 "):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01fd6178-40df-4a0b-9e65-56e5ec294f18"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fdKinetic", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nn_", ",", " ", "dx_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dx", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
     RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"i_", ",", " ", "i_"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "2."}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"i_", ",", " ", "j_"}], "}"}], " ", "/;", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "j"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            "1"}]}], " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "1."}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7364bd1a-a61f-42e3-9730-d0a1fe8982b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The process itself stacks the real and imaginary parts of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07f222ae-e417-493d-841f-9602370e0575"],
 " into one real state vector, with the drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "97bfcbd3-05d2-4b8e-890c-1d24c01ec082"],
 " and the scalar-noise diffusion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "216f3d85-cfb8-424e-a163-2af33bf30f74"],
 " read directly from the SSE:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6adb7963-0a51-49f5-8366-e430f3dae7f1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sseProcess", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0_"}], "]"}], " ", 
   ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"xs", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kmat", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"fdKinetic", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<dx\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "us", ",",
        " ", "vs", ",", " ", "xav", ",", " ", "a", ",", " ", "drift", ",", 
       " ", "diff"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"us", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Unique", "[", "\"\<u\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"vs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Unique", "[", "\"\<v\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"xav", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xs", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"us", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vs", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xs", " ", "-", " ", "xav"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"drift", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"kmat", " ", ".", " ", "vs"}], "/", "hbar"}], " ", "-", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], " ", "us"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", 
            RowBox[{"kmat", " ", ".", " ", "us"}]}], "/", "hbar"}], " ", "-", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], " ", "vs"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"diff", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "us"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "vs"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"drift", ",", " ", "diff"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{"us", ",", " ", "vs"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Re", "@", "\[Psi]0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Im", "@", "\[Psi]0"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"776c79b0-2e33-40b0-8505-dccf0addccd8"],

Cell["\<\
Choose a small grid the built-in can afford, and an initial packet:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a01a115-83ed-4270-911a-be2d9c5ba911"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"24", ",", " ", "12."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]I", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gI", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], ";",
   " ", 
  RowBox[{"nI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gI", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"74ef7239-db1f-4531-8a7b-29eb6bb3b037"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Integrate four hundred trajectories with ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b4766075-2782-4edc-be3c-f8faf28b5b0f"],
 ", using the scalar-noise stochastic Runge-Kutta method:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68c6c78b-8851-48cc-85f6-34400bb1869e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tdIto", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sseProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gI", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "\[Psi]I"}], "]"}], ",",
        "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dtS"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "400", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "Method", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b5c38bc7-1e78-4b83-a246-f7d14a75ebe3"],

Cell["\<\
Reassemble each final real state vector into a complex wavefunction:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85450594-9854-440e-ab21-c454e09c8c6d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"itoFinals", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{";;", " ", "nI"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", 
        RowBox[{"#", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"nI", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], 
      ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"tdIto", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"43771b0d-e122-4a71-8f11-5db0e1042616"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For comparison, represent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1fc6e717-cdb4-4d64-9857-8f2425459b59"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed643921-8923-46eb-a93d-ad0179a9213c"],
 " as matrices on this grid:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a097f567-696e-4529-bb82-e7de300e423b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xmI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gI", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"p2mI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", 
    RowBox[{"fdKinetic", "[", 
     RowBox[{"nI", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gI", "[", "\"\<dx\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8f93aa5b-fb5b-498d-ad67-c15408f566a8"],

Cell["\<\
Average the built-in trajectories into a density matrix, renormalizing each \
first since its norm has drifted:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57ce135d-b488-4865-a7d8-25c52dc71282"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"itoRho", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
      " ", "itoFinals"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e15860be-e825-4772-99e4-caa2fe2e2946"],

Cell["\<\
Compare the built-in's norm drift and observables against the same analytic \
master-equation moments:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e8c9b52-29e1-4279-b4b6-438e1e9123e2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<ItoProcess norm drift\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<ItoProcess {\:27e8x\.b2\:27e9, \:27e8p\.b2\:27e9, purity}\>\"",
      ",", " ", "\"\<master equation {\:27e8x\.b2\:27e9, \:27e8p\.b2\:27e9}\>\
\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
         "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "itoFinals"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"itoRho", " ", ".", " ", "xmI", " ", ".", " ", "xmI"}], 
         "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"itoRho", " ", ".", " ", "p2mI"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"itoRho", " ", ".", " ", "itoRho"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", "moments"}], 
      " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"v0", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"q0", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]I", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "p2mI", 
           " ", ".", " ", "\[Psi]I"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{"m", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", "tf"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"52358d3c-05df-4466-a7f7-3b01ab3ad458"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The built-in reproduces the physics: its ensemble matches the \
master-equation moments within Monte-Carlo scatter, and it decoheres to the \
same mixed purity. But it is the coarser tool here, for two reasons, both \
traced to the measured operator. A general-purpose integrator does not \
preserve the nonlinear norm invariant of the SSE, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleVerticalBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7abfe3dd-22b5-4228-9318-46fae56cae38"],
 " departs from ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a4d9706-53c7-4f3e-b247-c7de9a264948"],
 " by about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["10", 
   RowBox[{"-", "4"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a215f0ac-627b-42c7-b547-82944a172f3c"],
 ", against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["10", 
   RowBox[{"-", "15"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd72720-a390-474f-ac66-aeceb78af392"],
 " for the split-operator scheme, and each trajectory must be renormalized \
before observables are evaluated. And because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "801e5128-fca3-455b-b71b-39cbc3892be2"],
 " is unbounded, the norm-preserving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99ee2aca-c3c3-48ac-9117-1bb16d5450c6"],
 " drift is stiff: it limits the step size, a limit that tightens as the grid \
grows, so the built-in can afford only a small grid with a finite-difference \
kinetic energy that slightly underestimates the backaction heating."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"928353db-361a-4cf7-b5ac-a94bd975a322"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Neither limitation is intrinsic to ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a7648f90-aac8-4ecc-ad17-fcb804ed7030"],
 ". Both follow from propagating the full state vector while the operator is \
unbounded; in the right coordinates the built-in is exact. A qubit trajectory \
simulator propagates not the state vector but the three Bloch components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96057e4d-0845-4ab8-81cd-ad2c00b730bd"],
 ", a complete parametrization of a two-level state, confined to the ball ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d97db65-6946-4342-bcaf-f19cefdea62c"],
 " that the stochastic master equation holds invariant, so positivity is \
enforced geometrically and no renormalization is required. The free particle \
admits the same reduction. Under continuous position measurement a Gaussian \
state remains Gaussian, so five real parameters suffice: the means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f6b0079-f529-4f95-b91d-6a7626f9efa2"],
 " and the covariances ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], ",", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7373dc66-96e8-432c-91ae-6134f916b2a7"],
 ", where only the means carry the Wiener noise and the covariances obey the \
deterministic Riccati flow of Part IV. This is the continuous quantum \
Kalman-Bucy filter. Supply its five parameters to ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c972b35a-dd89-4122-b0c3-afad92abacb0"],
 " in place of the grid:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"278ace20-c517-4872-ac5f-8dc511a9c03a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"momentProc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"mp", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"vp", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
        "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"mx", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mp", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"vp", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "mx", ",", " ", "mp", ",", " ", "vx", ",", " ", "vc", ",", " ", 
         "vp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
         "0.25"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[46]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6fe73a6f-0da4-409e-b8d1-17806fbe64d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Normalization is now automatic, since there is no unnormalized state \
vector: the conditional state is Gaussian by construction. The purity \
invariant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eee17b78-151a-41e7-983c-fe2063a71c63"],
 " replaces the norm, and its deterministic flow has an attracting fixed \
point at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7640f516-7b36-4892-a8be-7132baead37d"],
 ", so numerical error is contracted rather than accumulated. Integrate at \
forty times the grid step, over four thousand realizations, and read the \
backaction heating and the purity error:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d056194e-5607-4575-a849-5cd11f76580b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tdM", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
      RowBox[{"momentProc", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "0.02"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "4000", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
       "Method", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"finM", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"tdM", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<purity error\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<E[\:27e8p\.b2\:27e9](tf)\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          "0.25"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "finM"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"#", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
        " ", "finM"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[47]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3589fe59-cf13-45ea-990e-45ece95ef215"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The purity invariant holds to about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "4"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50cceae1-8f74-43fc-8252-26ded255009a"],
 " at that coarse step, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "088499f7-d771-40bd-a294-82911228f101"],
 " reaches the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0.25", "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["f", "TI"]], "=", "0.65"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657554e3-3f54-4f89-a19e-a3f040775fa5"],
 " as the master equation, with no renormalization. The built-in is now as \
accurate here as for a qubit, and for the same reason: a complete, \
low-dimensional parametrization whose single constraint the flow preserves \
autonomously."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a494ec59-4eea-44db-9da8-7b864c3d1e44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This reduction is the special case, not the general tool. The \
five-parameter description exists only because the free particle is a linear \
(Gaussian) system, so the moment hierarchy closes; introduce a potential in \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "629f9864-ea43-4222-bf48-e0855f7ed786"],
 " and it does not close, the conditional state is no longer Gaussian, and \
only the grid split-operator scheme applies. This sets the division of labor. \
When the conditional state lies in a small closed parametrization, a qubit's \
Bloch vector or a Gaussian's moments, the built-in integrator suffices and \
the geometry preserves physicality. Otherwise, hand-write the step whose \
structure can be exploited, here the exact Kraus operator with its \
renormalization, which is independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e1e2d62-3089-41d4-b906-239a5c86d57c"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0225f0cc-38d0-41c0-9319-75de3a0f1572"],

Cell["Part VII: The Simulation-to-Experiment Dictionary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9d293d87-cbe7-4c9c-89e0-81dd244aa63c"],

Cell["\<\
Every simulated quantity has an experimental counterpart. The correspondence \
is collected here.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90cb79d9-cae2-4f03-b8f7-d4063b58f3ef"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["In the simulation", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"d8fbcca8-2e57-493d-af81-10e47990352a"],
     Cell["Experimental counterpart", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"29c7e1d5-dce7-43c3-9212-691cad520137"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "the record, the outcomes ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "5bb22471-39a0-42df-b89e-15eb3202cf8c"],
     " (or ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "4e0f33e5-86c9-4ff4-95ae-6eb870013805"],
     ")"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"39511d1e-7a31-4554-a0e4-5da3789f7d8a"], 
    Cell["\<\
the homodyne photocurrent, a continuous noisy position readout\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b1739005-34d4-48be-a0be-bc28436e4eb7"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "one trajectory ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
       "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "de6c3c71-d04d-4290-837f-3521f2509307"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4c639fc7-dfdc-44d8-9aec-c7e6dc9705d1"], 
    Cell["\<\
the conditional state in one run, reconstructed by filtering the photocurrent\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8585314b-3058-4a4b-bfdc-dd461a5bf87d"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "the conditional mean ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "a2d57192-408d-45bc-aa43-6bf3e5ea1188"],
     ", red curve"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"240b9df0-efa3-46d7-8f57-5f0a71aa0518"], 
    Cell["the filtered position estimate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "28b82945-7080-427e-9e39-c48e11f7c9dd"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "the conditional variance ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "9b17ced5-b8e7-40f7-9ad2-42394b3b35cb"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"d528c83a-eef0-4abb-8cdf-2acf71765b6f"], 
    Cell["the residual (a-posteriori) position uncertainty", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"a847085a-8685-4e09-85b7-e19772858095"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "trajectory purity ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "3c34d92e-8359-418b-bf83-057ba830a20a"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f305face-b841-447e-8085-11b47feafdf1"], 
    Cell["\<\
at unit efficiency, monitoring keeps the conditional state pure\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e49a132f-b523-47e1-9e42-5a1527840306"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "the unconditional ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "7e5bee7c-d06a-4969-a635-f48cae4e6426"],
     ", purity ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "27207000-052a-4c59-b5f0-8e8a50bf61fa"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a4ac2204-9cbd-45f3-bb58-f15cbadc9140"], 
    Cell["\<\
the state when the record is discarded: the mixed, decohered master-equation \
state\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ed975ef1-53e0-49ac-9261-2398034418f7"]},
   {Cell["ensemble spread of trajectories", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "43fdbcdc-7a03-4720-b994-99cc2d07be0e"], Cell[
    "the shot-to-shot scatter of repeated experiments", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"ea0e85f3-df72-4a21-96bc-8583e67f22dc"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "b74c23a6-a8ad-494a-9f42-19be70adc42c"],
     " growing as ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "198edf5f-8175-4a19-ae50-d27ced9bf512"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5c1e50fc-7014-45f0-84c8-226955c1093a"], 
    Cell["\<\
measurement backaction, the momentum diffusion driving the standard quantum \
limit\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8de48ca5-cb86-414e-bcd0-f8b5fe7616f6"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.44], 
      Scaled[0.44]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",Express\
ionUUID->"5b8d5921-a196-433a-8553-c062ae372966"],

Cell["\<\
The organizing principle: the master equation is the a-priori state, averaged \
over every outcome the detector could return; a single trajectory is the \
a-posteriori state conditioned on one realized record. Filtering the record \
to reconstruct the conditional state is exactly what a real-time monitoring \
or feedback experiment does; discarding it leaves the unconditional, \
decohering state. The simulation provides both, and exposes the pure \
conditional trajectories comprising the mixed unconditional average.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66e71d32-5ccd-4a22-b28a-950148f71d1c"],

Cell["Part VIII: Comparison with Experiment", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6ba547c9-d5a3-4887-b605-2b188f89a1f5"],

Cell["\<\
The free particle under continuous position measurement is an idealization, \
but its measurement-theoretic content is realized directly in cavity and \
levitated optomechanics, where the position of a mechanical oscillator is \
monitored continuously by scattered or cavity light. The correspondence is \
exact for the measurement, and the numbers below are taken from two \
experiments that reconstruct a mechanical resonator's quantum trajectory from \
its measurement record.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4de5c41f-9d31-4267-9818-0a7e7c1a0ec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In Magrini et al. (Nature ",
 StyleBox["595",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 373 (2021), ",
 ButtonBox["arXiv:2012.15188",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.15188"], None}],
 "), an optically levitated nanoparticle is monitored by position-resolving \
light near the Heisenberg imprecision-backaction limit, and its motional \
quantum state is reconstructed in real time by a Kalman filter, the classical \
name for the continuous quantum filter of Part VI. The filter output is the \
experimental analogue of the red curve: the conditional mean and variance \
propagated from the photocurrent. The reported conditional position \
uncertainty is ",
 Cell[BoxData["1.3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8611d044-5e6f-42e7-b5cd-8cd23b68057b"],
 " times the zero-point value, and feedback on the estimate cools the \
oscillator to a mean occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0.56", "\[PlusMinus]", "0.02"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "667f12a8-a496-4371-b8fb-005907b164b4"],
 ", its motional ground state, from room temperature. Rossi et al. (Nature ",
 StyleBox["563",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 53 (2018), ",
 ButtonBox["arXiv:1805.05087",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.05087"], None}],
 "; and the companion Phys. Rev. Lett. ",
 StyleBox["123",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 163601 (2019), \"Observing and verifying the quantum trajectory of a \
mechanical resonator\") perform the same continuous position measurement on a \
soft-clamped membrane at near-unit measurement efficiency, reconstruct the \
conditional state by causal Wiener/Kalman filtering, reach a conditional \
occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0.29", "\[PlusMinus]", "0.03"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01d418fa-7005-4365-81b2-5a704e6f0848"],
 ", and operate ",
 Cell[BoxData["9"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ff444ec5-8edf-4aff-aad1-77e4385e5a1a"],
 " dB below the quantum backaction limit of sideband cooling."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"683a230e-e4f3-4afb-82f6-f9215ab23335"],

Cell["The quantities carrying measured values map as follows:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9a5fd7cc-247a-4519-a193-66155782edf7"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Simulated quantity", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"dc90590c-07eb-47d1-97b7-cd06a9c2428a"],
     Cell["Measured value", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"cf2d76ae-c196-43e1-bd6e-2137e38b05ce"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "the record ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "5a6937a8-a4af-487a-b908-814c32c029df"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"46fb0ee9-724d-4a2d-849a-5467ff829b3a"], 
    Cell["the homodyne photocurrent of the scattered/cavity light", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2be8ca6e-3394-410c-bb17-78297089b7ca"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "conditional mean and variance ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "5ca34fdb-ecb5-4e04-8e07-401ef5b02b14"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b8015deb-ba14-459c-ace0-655a2d57b142"], 
    Cell["the real-time Kalman-filter estimate and its covariance", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c0e7ff2d-5a2b-4c31-b2d0-66d29b6d25cf"]},
   {Cell["steady conditional position uncertainty", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"c8e9b92c-d6bc-401a-afa4-dc25032a2424"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"1.3", "\[Times]"}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "1908190e-8074-48f4-98ee-87d4ddfb4143"],
     " zero-point (Magrini 2021)"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b5b038bd-246e-4e86-9bf3-613efd491c0a"]},
   {Cell["conditional occupation reached by feedback", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"8298011a-d547-4a0e-a201-008043fc1eba"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0.56", "\[PlusMinus]", "0.02"}]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "ed273597-eedb-4633-a090-48ae2b851923"],
     " (Magrini), ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0.29", "\[PlusMinus]", "0.03"}]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "a82fe347-9608-480c-a539-5e319f356f3d"],
     " (Rossi)"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"42919574-438e-42d0-aaf3-b208b5908915"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "measurement efficiency ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "db4e504d-5066-4066-9628-da27ab637d31"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1760f2a3-9201-4bf2-ade1-90e046b093fd"], 
    Cell[TextData[{
     "near unity (Rossi); sub-unity ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "bcec5630-ffa5-45de-a5d2-699560fa0c5b"],
     " gives conditional purity below one"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"20c7c980-dfd9-45aa-8ddf-a62c957ec0b9"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "backaction heating ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "8020d430-8526-428e-9e35-30fe93ffcfda"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"34143358-cf49-4ee5-9d42-6c7978db0b6b"], 
    Cell[TextData[{
     "radiation-pressure backaction, ",
     Cell[BoxData["9"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "73735dd9-dfe3-44ad-9fc8-038fbb8437b4"],
     " dB below the sideband-cooling backaction limit (Rossi)"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"eb5ce74c-80a8-48ca-9a6d-3925673c181e"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.44], 
      Scaled[0.44]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",Express\
ionUUID->"55f305c4-0cff-45e8-8d99-df1825064b0f"],

Cell["\<\
The Part VI moment filter is not merely analogous to these experiments; it is \
the identical algorithm. Both propagate a Gaussian conditional state by the \
continuous quantum Kalman-Bucy equations, the means driven by the record and \
the covariances following a deterministic Riccati flow, and the experiments \
run exactly this on a field-programmable gate array in real time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5365899-c65f-45c3-86c5-db5a970e3e49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two qualifications are needed. First, the particle here is free, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec16e1d1-7c41-4432-ac22-377bad4f8bd0"],
 ", whereas these oscillators are harmonically trapped: the measurement \
machinery, the SSE, the record, the Kalman filter, the backaction, and the \
conditional-unconditional split, transfers unchanged, but the trap adds a \
restoring term to the drift, so the steady conditional variance is set by the \
ratio of the measurement rate to the mechanical and thermal rates rather than \
by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fa8e0f0a-e12a-43da-a7e8-fc1968b2805e"],
 ". Second, the experiments run at efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2e52fbb-609b-47e6-bab9-13627a85b2cf"],
 ": some scattered light is lost, so the reconstructed conditional state is \
mixed and its purity is below one, whereas the simulation at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ad5ce5f1-fe40-4a44-b214-3e3f073ff9f8"],
 " produces pure conditional trajectories. Restoring ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a9b82db1-ebac-433a-9afb-710574d5a6ae"],
 " in the simulation, which replaces the pure-state SSE by a stochastic \
master equation for a conditional density matrix, reproduces the sub-unity \
conditional purity these experiments report, and is the extension flagged \
below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd1d5a16-cad1-48d1-ab07-2b0c2be5a66e"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"08c5edc3-cbe7-4005-bb20-417b6c31a08e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The full loop is now in runnable form: a detector model emitting a \
stochastic record, one realization mapping a record to a pure conditional \
trajectory whose mean diffuses while its variance localizes, an ensemble \
whose average reproduces the Lindblad master equation as a mixture of those \
pure conditional states, and the exact backaction heating rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "97d13d84-d0c6-4737-af1b-fc8d7bfc4bcc"],
 " that measurement pays for position information. The most consequential \
parameter is the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "433db1fd-8156-44e6-bbc9-508b272d9260"],
 ": reduce it and the conditional state barely responds while the record \
remains shot-noise dominated; increase it and the conditional state localizes \
to the steady width almost immediately while the momentum heats faster than a \
coarse grid can represent. The natural extensions are to reduce the detection \
efficiency below unity, so that a single record no longer purifies the \
conditional state and the trajectory becomes a mixed conditional density \
matrix, or to add a potential to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a8445da-e01c-4fd1-888c-657251a8578a"],
 " and study the same record-conditioned dynamics in a trap, the setting of \
cavity optomechanics."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43d4f245-63ec-4ba3-a833-8a2f3a68f3aa"]
},
CreateCellID->True,
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
